      "title": "Admissions Assistant",
      "description": "Admissions Assistant - Term | Career Opportunities Skip to main content Toggle Navigation Find Opportunities U.S. English British English CA English Danish Deutsch Dutch Español FR French Français Canadien Italian Português do Brasil Swedish U.S. English 简体中文 Sign In Post Admissions Assistant - Term Job Category : Administrative Staff Requisition Number : ADMIS001739 Quick apply Posting Details Posted : August 21, 2026 Full-Time On-site Locations Showing 1 location Nova Scotia St. Francis Xavier University 4130 University Avenue Antigonish, NS B2G2W5, CAN Nova Scotia St. Francis Xavier University 4130 University Avenue Antigonish, NS B2G2W5, CAN +0 more locations less locations Job Details Description Position Title: Admissions Assistant Department: Recruitment & Admissions Position Type: Full-Time (Term - ends January 29, 2027) Classification: NSGEU, Band 4 Salary Range: $21.44/hour - $26.20/hour Posting Date: August 21, 2026 Closing Date: September 1, 2026, at 1:00 PM AST Position Description St Francis Xavier University, which offers Canada’s premier undergraduate experience, is seeking an Academic Services Assistant to join the Admissions Office for a full-time, term position. Reporting to the Associate Registrar, Admissions, this person will be a member of an integrated team working in a collaborative, shared work environment, providing superior service to prospective and current StFX students. Key Responsibilities Correspond via email, telephone, and in person with various stakeholders (prospective students, parents, guidance counsellors, internal contacts, International Recruitment Agencies, etc.) regarding StFX, its programs, and the admissions process. Receive and process admissions applications and supporting documents with a high level of efficiency and accuracy, including verifying data of electronic applications, entering manual applications, and uploading all supporting documents (transcripts, language tests, and other supplemental information). Confirm with students the specific documentation received and the necessary documents outstanding to be submitted. Ensure accurate data entry for updating file information such as name, address, email changes, program change requests, etc. Process application change forms, deferral requests, and application withdrawals and correspond with appropriate StFX personnel informing them of the same. Qualifications Completion of a post-secondary certificate or diploma in a related field (office administration, business) or equivalent experience. Ability to complete repetitive tasks with a high degree of accuracy and attention to detail. Demonstrated experience and ability working in a time-sensitive and high-volume environment with changing and conflicting priorities and frequent interruptions. Superb customer service skills with demonstrated excellence in customer service communication. Proficiency working in an Office 365 environment.  Familiarity and experience with student information systems (Banner) and application / CRM software (TargetX/Salesforce) are considered an asset. The ability to work well with others and maintain cooperative and effective working relationships in a team environment. To apply for this opportunity, click the \" Quick Apply \" button and upload your cover letter and resume as a single combined PDF document (maximum 6 MB). Only one file can be uploaded per application. StFX is located in Mi’kma’ki, the ancestral and unceded territory of the Mi’kmaq People. Our institution is committed to upholding the values of equity, diversity, inclusion and accessibility. We encourage applications from members of groups that have been historically disadvantaged and marginalized, including Indigenous persons (especially Mi’kmaq), racialized persons (especially African Nova Scotians), persons with disabilities, those who identify as women and/or 2SLGBTQIA+ and any others who would contribute to the diversity of our community. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. We are also committed to the elimination of barriers to participation for persons with disabilities. Should you require an accommodation during the recruitment process, please contact People and Culture at hr@stfx.ca or 902-867-5038. About the Admissions Office The Admissions Department at StFX is responsible for guiding prospective students through the university application and admissions process.  We provide information on academic programs, admissions requirements, application procedures, scholarships, and key deadlines.  We support students from their initial inquiry through to receiving an admissions offer and acceptance. About St. Francis Xavier University Established in 1853, St. Francis Xavier University (StFX) is consistently recognized as one of the best universities in Canada. StFX exceeds the needs of today’s undergraduates by providing the very best academic experience -- outstanding teaching, exceptional hands-on research opportunities, and global exchanges -- all within Canada’s most vibrant and inspiring residential campus. Here, the focus is on the academic and personal development of every student, making community and social engagement a large part of the learning experience. Our students are academically strong and highly engaged in every aspect of life, determined to make a positive impact on the world. In 2022, Maclean's annual university rankings put StFX #1 in student satisfaction and #2 in reputation across Canada in the primarily undergraduate category. For more, visit www.stfx.ca . About Antigonish, Nova Scotia The beautiful and historic town of Antigonish is located within the northeastern corner of Nova Scotia. Only a 15-minute drive from the ocean and a two-hour drive to major urban centres, Antigonish is a family-friendly community with a diverse and growing population and provides access to excellent education at all levels. The town is surrounded by rolling countryside and beautiful beaches and is a hotspot for outdoor recreation, sports and other active lifestyle activities. Antigonish supports a vibrant culture in the arts with music, performing arts, visual arts and crafts, and fabulous festivals happening throughout the year. For more information visit www.townofantigonish.ca or www.visitantigonish.ca . Qualifications Skills Behaviors : Motivations : Education Experience Licenses & Certifications St. Francis Xavier University You are using an unsupported browser. To use this site, please use a supported browser. Download Firefox Download Chrome Download Internet Explorer"
    },
    "https://recruiting.ultipro.ca/GOV5000GOVE/JobBoard/b0aac1dd-538d-4eb2-91aa-e8ce062974c9/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=ea769db9-1182-48d5-bc02-9ef34f264704": {
      "title": "Institutional Attendant II",
      "description": "Institutional Attendant II - Transportation | Career Opportunities Skip to main content Toggle Navigation Find Opportunities U.S. English British English CA English Danish Deutsch Dutch Español FR French Français Canadien Italian Português do Brasil Swedish U.S. English 简体中文 Sign In Post Institutional Attendant II - Transportation Job Category : Facilities Management Requisition Number : INSTI001738 Apply now Posting Details Posted : August 20, 2026 Full-Time On-site Rate : $21.57 CAD per hour Locations Showing 1 location Nova Scotia St. Francis Xavier University 4130 University Avenue Antigonish, NS B2G2W5, CAN Nova Scotia St. Francis Xavier University 4130 University Avenue Antigonish, NS B2G2W5, CAN +0 more locations less locations Job Details Description The Transport IAII provides transportation, moving, mail and operational support across the StFX campus. The position requires a dependable, safety-conscious and adaptable individual who can work independently and as part of the Grounds & Transport team. While transportation and mail services are the primary focus of this position, the successful candidate will be expected to cross-train and provide support across Grounds & Transport operations, including snow and ice management, as operational needs require. Priorities may change in response to weather, campus events, emergencies, staffing requirements and other operational demands. Job Duties: Load, unload and transport furniture, equipment, materials and supplies between campus buildings and off-campus storage sites, including delivery and retrieval for University events and operational activities. Provide campus mail and scheduled delivery services, including the pickup, sorting, transportation and delivery of mail, materials and other approved items. Pick up and deliver supplies, materials and equipment for Facilities Management personnel and other approved University operational requirements. Operate snow removal equipment and perform manual snow and ice removal as required. Organize and carry out assigned transportation and moving requests efficiently, adjusting work as priorities and operational requirements change. Track completed moving and transportation requests and report exceptions, damage, safety concerns or incomplete work. Safely operate University vehicles, trucks, trailers, material-handling equipment and other equipment as trained and authorized. Perform routine inspections of assigned vehicles and equipment and report maintenance, repair or safety concerns. Provide flexible support across Grounds & Transport operations, including cross-training and semi-skilled work in other areas as assigned. Perform other related duties consistent with the classification as assigned. Normal Shift: 8:00 a.m. – 4:00 p.m., Monday to Friday. Flexibility in scheduling is an important requirement of this position. Operational requirements, particularly snow and ice response, may require work outside regular hours, including early mornings, evenings, nights and weekends. Employees are expected to participate in snow and ice operations as required. Skills, Education and Abilities Requirements: Minimum Grade 12 or GED equivalent education. Experience operating trucks, trailers, heavy equipment and/or mobile equipment. Experience in grounds, transportation, moving, delivery, facilities or similar operational services would be an asset. Must be able to obtain required certification for forklift and Trackless snowplough operation through an approved third-party training provider. This may include applicable sight and hearing requirements. Must possess a valid driver's licence Ability to safely lift and manoeuvre a minimum of 25 kg. Ability to perform basic mechanical inspections and minor maintenance of vehicles and equipment within the scope of the position. Ability to understand and follow technical instructions, operating manuals, procedures and safe work practices. Ability to use a tablet or other mobile device to receive work assignments, enter basic information and update the status of assigned work. Demonstrated reliability, punctuality and commitment to safe work practices, with the ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team. Strong organizational, time-management and problem-solving skills, with the ability to exercise sound judgement and adapt as operational priorities change. Strong interpersonal and customer-service skills when interacting with students, faculty, staff and other members of the University community. Willingness and ability to learn new tasks, cross-train and provide support across Grounds & Transport functions. Ability to work safely and effectively in changing weather conditions and physically demanding environments. Additional requirement The successful candidate will be required to provide: A satisfactory Driver’s Abstract. A satisfactory Criminal Record Check, including a Vulnerable Sector Check. Costs associated with obtaining the required Driver’s Abstract, Criminal Record Check and Vulnerable Sector Check will be reimbursed by the University. To apply for this opportunity, click the \" Quick Apply \" button and upload your cover letter and resume as a single combined PDF document (maximum 6 MB). Only one file can be uploaded per application. St. Francis Xavier University is located in Mi’kma’ki, the ancestral and unceded territory of the Mi’kmaq People. StFX is seeking candidates who are committed to contributing to our priorities of equity, diversity, and inclusion. A demonstrated ability in fostering a climate of inclusion and cultural safety is a strong asset. Preference will be given to applicants who bring lived experience of historically excluded groups. We are also committed to the elimination of barriers to participation for persons with disabilities. Should you require an accommodation during the recruitment process, please contact People and Culture at hr@stfx.ca or 902-867-5038. Qualifications Skills Behaviors : Motivations : Education Experience Licenses & Certifications St. Francis Xavier University You are using an unsupported browser. To use this site, please use a supported browser. Download Firefox Download Chrome Download Internet Explorer"
    },
    "https://recruiting.ultipro.ca/GOV5000GOVE/JobBoard/b0aac1dd-538d-4eb2-91aa-e8ce062974c9/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=fe0995dd-023e-4039-a2fa-4908f1feae10": {
      "title": "Outreach & Engagement Librarian, Limited Term Appointment",
      "description": "Outreach & Engagement Librarian, Limited Term Appointment | Career Opportunities Skip to main content Toggle Navigation Find Opportunities U.S. English British English CA English Danish Deutsch Dutch Español FR French Français Canadien Italian Português do Brasil Swedish U.S. English 简体中文 Sign In Post Outreach & Engagement Librarian, Limited Term Appointment Job Category : Faculty and Academic Staff Requisition Number : ACADE001719 Apply now Posting Details Posted : August 4, 2026 Full-Time On-site Locations Showing 1 location Nova Scotia St. Francis Xavier University 4130 University Avenue Antigonish, NS B2G2W5, CAN Nova Scotia St. Francis Xavier University 4130 University Avenue Antigonish, NS B2G2W5, CAN +0 more locations less locations Job Details Description The Angus L. Macdonald Library, St. Francis Xavier University (StFX), seeks a collaborative, innovative, and student-centered librarian to lead our outreach and engagement programs and services. This 8-month limited term position will be filled at the rank of Librarian I or II, with a start date by the end of September 2026. The Angus L. Macdonald Library serves one of Canada's top-ranked undergraduate educational institutions and sees its role as a proactive one of service and support for the academic success of its students and faculty. The library is a member of Novanet, a consortium of Nova Scotia academic libraries sharing a common library management system, the Council of Atlantic Academic Libraries (CAAL), and the Canadian Research Knowledge Network (CRKN), among other collaborative initiatives.  As members of the Faculty Union, Librarians must demonstrate a record of professional and scholarly activities. Position Description Reporting to the University Librarian, the successful candidate will establish partnerships with the Diversity Engagement Centre, academic departments, student organizations, and other campus units to identify opportunities for collaborative programming. The Outreach & Engagement Librarian will create programs and services to engage traditionally underrepresented campus populations. They will promote library spaces and services and create opportunities for academic conversations, research collaborations, and social engagements. With a deep understanding of the challenges of diversity and equity in higher education, this librarian leads the library’s outreach activities to increase connections on campus, with a specific focus on the following communities: Indigenous, Black, first generation, 2SLGBTQIA+, and international students and faculty. The successful candidate will participate in library services, including regularly scheduled reference desk shifts; and will serve as Liaison Librarian to designated departments and/or programs, providing specialized information literacy instruction, research assistance, and support for library resource selection and evaluation to those departments. Other duties include, but are not limited to, participation in library committees, initiatives, and projects, the creation and maintenance of subject research guides, and the creation and delivery of library workshops. Responsibilities: Develop partnerships and identify opportunities for collaborative programming; Manage and implement the library’s social media and communications strategy; Promote the library’s resources, services and spaces to students and faculty; Assess and work to improve the library’s online presence to ensure its continued currency, effectiveness, and usability, with a specific focus on diversity, inclusion, and accessibility; Develop and manage library outreach initiatives to university and community audiences; Formulate and action goals, plans, and procedures for implementing outreach services; Gather and analyze statistics and prepare evaluative reports for outreach and engagement programs; Assess user experience with resources, services, and space; Organize, promote, and host library programming; Coordinate and schedule library instruction that is not discipline-specific (open workshops), including delivery of some workshops; Promote library resources and services at university open houses, new student orientations, and other public events; Provide library tours and orientation to visiting scholars and students. Required Qualifications A Master’s degree in Library/Information Studies or equivalent from an ALA-accredited program; Demonstrated relevant knowledge or experience in advancing diversity, equity, inclusion and awareness in libraries or educational institutions; Demonstrated relevant knowledge or experience providing online and in-person reference support, information literacy instruction, and collection development, preferably in an academic library environment; Availability for occasional evening and weekend work; Proficiency with Microsoft products (Outlook, Word, Excel, OneDrive, Teams); An understanding of current and emerging technologies and techniques to achieve the library’s outreach and engagement objectives; Demonstrated ability to work both collaboratively in a team environment and independently on assigned responsibilities; Demonstrated understanding of EDIA principles and their importance in an academic institution and an academic library; Excellent communication, organizational, and time management skills. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of effective program development, including goal setting and outcomes evaluation; Experience discussing and presenting on sensitive topics to varied audiences, assessing training and support needs; Exceptional interpersonal skills, with the ability to establish positive and productive collaborations working with diverse audiences and colleagues; Familiarity with ExLibris Primo/Alma ILS and SpringShare products; Knowledge of graphic design principles or demonstrated aptitude; Experience using social media for outreach and/or engagement; Experience in community-based work with underrepresented youth, and a deep understanding of the unique challenges faced by these populations in a university setting; Understanding of the importance of professional growth, academic service, and scholarly activity in an academic environment. Review of applications will begin on August 12, 2026. To express interest in this role, please send a cover letter and CV in confidence to: Carolyn DeLorey, Interim University Librarian StFX University liboffice@stfx.ca St. Francis Xavier University is located in Mi’kma’ki, the ancestral and unceded territory of the Mi’kmaq People. Our institution is committed to upholding the values of equity, diversity, inclusion and accessibility. We encourage applications from members of groups that have been historically disadvantaged and marginalized, including Indigenous persons (especially Mi’kmaq), minoritized persons (especially African Nova Scotians), persons with disabilities, those who identify as women and/or 2SLGBTQIA+ and any others who would contribute to the diversity of our community. Qualified candidates may be provided the opportunity to self-identify through a process with People & Culture. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. We are also committed to the elimination of barriers to participation for persons with disabilities. Should you require an accommodation during the recruitment process, please contact People & Culture at hr@stfx.ca or 902- 867-5038. About St. Francis Xavier University StFX is a top-ranking Canadian, primarily undergraduate university focused on academic excellence, innovation in teaching and research, service to society and international outreach. Founded in 1853, StFX has a long and proud tradition as one of Canada’s oldest universities. For almost 165 years, we have cultivated our strong and resilient spirit, dedication to intellectual rigour, and commitment to engaging students who aspire to be community-minded citizens of the world. About Antigonish, Nova Scotia The beautiful and historic town of Antigonish, Nova Scotia, is located the northeastern corner of Nova Scotia. We’re only a 15-minute drive from the ocean and two-hour drive to major urban centres. With a diverse and growing population, Antigonish is a family friendly town with lots of opportunity, access to good education at all levels, recreation, sports and culture activities. It is surrounded by rolling countryside with hiking and beautiful beaches. We enjoy a vibrant culture in the arts with music, performing arts, visual arts and crafts, and fabulous festivals throughout the year. For more information, visit www.townofantigonish.ca or www.visitantigonish.ca Qualifications Skills Behaviors : Motivations : Education Experience Licenses & Certifications St. Francis Xavier University You are using an unsupported browser. To use this site, please use a supported browser. Download Firefox Download Chrome Download Internet Explorer"
    },
    "https://recruiting.ultipro.ca/GOV5000GOVE/JobBoard/b0aac1dd-538d-4eb2-91aa-e8ce062974c9/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=ac8fa21c-b498-4ebb-8f15-ba931808fd1c": {
      "title": "Research, Data and Evaluation Analyst, Collective Impact Initiative",
      "description": "Research, Data and Evaluation Analyst, Collective Impact Initiative | Career Opportunities Skip to main content Toggle Navigation Find Opportunities U.S. English British English CA English Danish Deutsch Dutch Español FR French Français Canadien Italian Português do Brasil Swedish U.S. English 简体中文 Sign In Post Research, Data and Evaluation Analyst, Collective Impact Initiative Job Category : Research Requisition Number : PROJE001730 Apply now Posting Details Posted : July 31, 2026 Full-Time On-site Locations Showing 1 location Nova Scotia St. Francis Xavier University 4130 University Avenue Antigonish, NS B2G2W5, CAN Nova Scotia St. Francis Xavier University 4130 University Avenue Antigonish, NS B2G2W5, CAN +0 more locations less locations Job Details Description Position Title: Research, Data and Evaluation Analyst Department: StFX Centre for Aging and Disability Justice Position Type: Part-time, 9-Month Term with possibility of renewal Salary Range: $33,000-42,000 (based on 22.5 hours/week) Posting Date: August 4, 2026 Closing Date: Applications will begin to be reviewed August 7, 2025. The position is open until filled St. Francis Xavier University is a top-ranking Canadian university focused on academic excellence, innovation in teaching and research, service to society and international outreach. The Centre for Aging and Disability Justice is a hub for research and public engagement on aging and disability justice. The Centre supports interdisciplinary, community-partnered, and first voice-led research that addresses critical policy issues, with a focus on rural communities. St. Francis Xavier University is seeking a Research, Data and Evaluation Analyst to support community-engaged research at the Centre on a Part-Time 9-month contract, with the possibility of renewal. The successful candidate will work independently, taking initiative to manage research and evaluation projects, meet timelines, and deliver high-quality research and evaluation outputs within a multi-year collective impact initiative. The role also involves collaboration with campus and community partners to support accessible and ethical research and evaluation practices. The position includes knowledge mobilization, translating research findings into accessible formats (e.g., reports, briefs, presentations), and sharing them with diverse audiences. This position is primarily in-person on the StFX campus, with the possibility of some remote work. Duties and Responsibilities Design and implement qualitative, quantitative, and mixed-methods research studies Develop and support data collection methods, including surveys (e.g., Qualtrics), interviews, and focus groups, in community-based contexts Conduct data analysis and ensure ethical, secure, and well-documented data management practices Lead and/or contribute to program evaluation and impact assessment activities Interpret and synthesize research findings for scholarly and applied purposes Produce high-quality written outputs and data visualizations for academic and non-academic audiences Contribute to knowledge mobilization activities, including dissemination and uptake of findings Support grant development, reporting requirements, and research ethics submissions Collaborate with project partners to strengthen capacity in data collection, analysis, and evidence-informed decision-makin Qualifications and Skills Undergraduate degree in social sciences, health sciences, data analysis, public administration, or a related field Minimum 3 years of relevant demonstrated experience in data analysis, research, evaluation, and reporting Demonstrated experience conducting qualitative, quantitative, and mixed-methods research Strong competencies in data management, statistical and/or qualitative analysis, and visualization Demonstrated ability to work independently and manage competing priorities within established timelines Proficiency with office software (e.g., Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint, databases) Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English Assets Graduate degree in a relevant field Experience in non-profit, community-based, or grant-funded research environments Familiarity with Mi’kmaw Ethics Watch review processes Application reviews will begin on August 7, 2026 and will continue until position is filled. To express your interest in this role, please send a cover letter describing your interest and relevant experiences and a resume or CV to: Dr. Katie Aubrecht & Dr. Megan MacGillivray at agingdisabilityjustice@stfx.ca Only those selected for an interview will be contacted. StFX is located in Mi’kma’ki, the ancestral and unceded territory of the Mi’kmaq People. Our institution is committed to upholding the values of equity, diversity, inclusion and accessibility. We encourage applications from members of groups that have been historically disadvantaged and marginalized, including Indigenous persons (especially Mi’kmaq), racialized persons (especially African Nova Scotians), persons with disabilities, those who identify as women and/or 2SLGBTQIA+ and any others who would contribute to the diversity of our community. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. We are also committed to the elimination of barriers to participation for persons with disabilities. Should you require an accommodation during the recruitment process, please contact People and Culture at hr@stfx.ca or 902-867-5038. Qualifications Skills Behaviors : Motivations : Education Experience Licenses & Certifications St. Francis Xavier University You are using an unsupported browser. To use this site, please use a supported browser. Download Firefox Download Chrome Download Internet Explorer"
    },
    "https://recruiting.ultipro.ca/GOV5000GOVE/JobBoard/b0aac1dd-538d-4eb2-91aa-e8ce062974c9/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=5bd77e8b-630b-4d51-bd67-3577611d4802": {
      "title": "Journeyman Steam & Pipefitter/Plumber",
      "description": "Journeyman Steam & Pipefitter/Plumber - Institutional Attendant IV | Career Opportunities Skip to main content Toggle Navigation Find Opportunities U.S. English British English CA English Danish Deutsch Dutch Español FR French Français Canadien Italian Português do Brasil Swedish U.S. English 简体中文 Sign In Post Journeyman Steam & Pipefitter/Plumber - Institutional Attendant IV Job Category : Facilities Management Requisition Number : JOURN001643 Apply now Posting Details Posted : July 27, 2026 Full-Time On-site Locations Showing 1 location Nova Scotia St. Francis Xavier University 4130 University Avenue Antigonish, NS B2G2W5, CAN Nova Scotia St. Francis Xavier University 4130 University Avenue Antigonish, NS B2G2W5, CAN +0 more locations less locations Job Details Description Position Title: Journeyman Steam & Pipefitter / Plumber IAIV Department: Facilities Management Position Type: Full-time, Permanent, 40 hours/week Classification: IAIV $31.64 Hourly / $65,811 Annually (for first 2080 hours) Reposted: August 24, 2026 Closing Date: Until Filled Reporting to the Mechanical and Electrical Supervisor, the Facilities Management Department is seeking a Journeyman Steamfitter & Pipefitter/Plumber with experience in maintenance and skilled trades work. The successful candidate will support the ongoing operation, repair, and maintenance of university systems and infrastructure. Key Responsibilities: Perform preventative and corrective maintenance on university equipment and building systems Complete installation of small projects, upgrades, and system modifications Participate in an on-call rotation shared among the maintenance team Maintain a valid driver’s license and operate university vehicles as required Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent Valid Journeyman Steamfitter & Pipefitter and/or Plumber certification A secondary trade certification or relevant cross-trade experience is considered an asset Demonstrated knowledge and experience in the installation and repair of heating, cooling, and process piping systems, including steam distribution systems (required) Experience with water distribution and sanitary drainage system installation and repair (required) Ability to perform semi-skilled work outside primary trade qualifications Proficiency in the safe use and maintenance of hand tools, power tools, and related equipment Ability to read and interpret technical drawings, schematics, and instructions Working knowledge of formulas, measurements, and conversion tables relevant to the trade Basic computer literacy To apply for this opportunity, click the \"Apply Now\" button and upload your cover letter, resume and references. StFX is located in Mi’kma’ki, the ancestral and unceded territory of the Mi’kmaq People. StFX is committed to equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility and encourages applications from individuals who will contribute to the diversity of our community. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. StFX is also committed to eliminating barriers to participation for persons with disabilities. If accommodation is required during the recruitment process, please contact People and Culture at hr@stfx.ca or 902-867-5038. Qualifications Skills Behaviors : Motivations : Education Experience Licenses & Certifications St. Francis Xavier University You are using an unsupported browser. To use this site, please use a supported browser. Download Firefox Download Chrome Download Internet Explorer"
    },
    "https://recruiting.ultipro.ca/GOV5000GOVE/JobBoard/b0aac1dd-538d-4eb2-91aa-e8ce062974c9/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=ced13d54-5f09-4511-b1e3-ed6483ebd14f": {
      "title": "The Antigonish Review - Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "The Antigonish Review - Administrative Assistant | Career Opportunities Skip to main content Toggle Navigation Find Opportunities U.S. English British English CA English Danish Deutsch Dutch Español FR French Français Canadien Italian Português do Brasil Swedish U.S. English 简体中文 Sign In Post The Antigonish Review - Administrative Assistant Job Category : Administrative Staff Requisition Number : THEAN001705 Apply now Posting Details Posted : July 14, 2026 Full-Time Hybrid Locations Showing 1 location Nova Scotia St. Francis Xavier University 4130 University Avenue Antigonish, NS B2G2W5, CAN Nova Scotia St. Francis Xavier University 4130 University Avenue Antigonish, NS B2G2W5, CAN +0 more locations less locations Job Details Description Position Title: The Antigonish Review - Administrative Assistant Department: Faculty of Arts / The Antigonish Review Position Type: Casual (10-12 hours/week) Classification: NSGEU, Band 3 Hourly Range: $19.75-24.12 Posting Date: July 13, 2026 Closing Date: September 2, 2026 Position Summary St. FX University is a Canadian university focused on academic excellence and is seeking an Administrative Assistant for the literary magazine The Antigonish Review . The Administrative Assistant is responsible for the magazine's day to day administrative duties, including general mail, budget tracking, and mail outs of the quarterly magazine. Key Responsibilities Perform administrative and financial functions, including managing the budget, invoices, contributor payments, subscriptions, and expense tracking. Coordinate magazine distribution, including mailing and liaison with printers. Organize promotional activities and special events, including advertising and cover art coordination. Prepare meeting materials, take minutes, maintain records, and provide general office administration and correspondence. Qualifications Diploma or degree in Publishing, English, Communications, Business Administration, Office Administration, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience with financial administration, including invoices, deposits, expense tracking, or bookkeeping. Experience using Excel spreadsheets (for managing mail outs and contributor payments). Experience providing administrative support in an editorial, publishing, communications, or professional office environment. Demonstrated organizational and interpersonal skills with the ability to communicate effectively. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively as part of a collaborative editorial team. Interest in literature, publishing, or the arts is considered an asset. To apply for this opportunity, click the \"Quick Apply\" button and upload your cover letter and resume as a single combined PDF document (maximum 6 MB). Only one file can be uploaded per application. StFX is located in Mi’kma’ki, the ancestral and unceded territory of the Mi’kmaq People. Our institution is committed to upholding the values of equity, diversity, inclusion and accessibility. We encourage applications from members of groups that have been historically disadvantaged and marginalized, including Indigenous persons (especially Mi’kmaq), racialized persons (especially African Nova Scotians), persons with disabilities, those who identify as women and/or 2SLGBTQIA+ and any others who would contribute to the diversity of our community. Please note that all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, applications from Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. We are also committed to the elimination of barriers to participation for persons with disabilities. Should you require an accommodation during the recruitment process, please contact People and Culture at hr@stfx.ca or 902-867-5038. About St. Francis Xavier University Established in 1853, St. Francis Xavier University (StFX) is consistently recognized as one of the best universities in Canada. StFX exceeds the needs of today’s undergraduates through providing the very best academic experience -- outstanding teaching, exceptional hands-on research opportunities, and global exchanges -- all within Canada’s most vibrant and inspiring residential campus. Here, the focus is on the academic and the personal development of every student, making community and social engagement a large part of the learning experience. Our students are academically strong and highly engaged in every aspect of life, determined to make a positive impact on the world. In 2026, Maclean's annual university rankings put StFX #1 for reputation across Canada in the primarily undergraduate category. For more, visit www.stfx.ca . About Antigonish, Nova Scotia The beautiful and historic town of Antigonish is located within the northeastern corner of Nova Scotia. Only a 15-minute drive from the ocean and a two-hour drive to major urban centres, Antigonish is a family-friendly community with a diverse and growing population and provides access to excellent education at all levels. The town is surrounded by rolling countryside and beautiful beaches and is a hotspot for outdoor recreation, sports and other active lifestyle activities. Antigonish supports a vibrant culture in the arts with music, performing arts, visual arts and crafts, and fabulous festivals happening throughout the year. For more information visit www.townofantigonish.ca o Qualifications Skills Behaviors : Motivations : Education Experience Licenses & Certifications St. Francis Xavier University You are using an unsupported browser. To use this site, please use a supported browser. Download Firefox Download Chrome Download Internet Explorer"
